<div class="terms-page container py-5">
  <div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 800px;">

    <header class="mb-5 text-center">
      <h1 class="terms-title font-orbitron text-haitian-blue mb-3">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="text-muted lead mx-auto" style="max-width: 640px;">
        These are the rules for using BonID. We wrote them in plain words so everyone can understand them.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="terms-summary mb-5">
      <h2 class="terms-summary-title">The short version</h2>
      <ul class="terms-list mb-0">
        <li>BonID helps you prove who you are, safely and online.</li>
        <li>Tell the truth and use only your own documents and your own face.</li>
        <li>Keep your account and your QR code to yourself.</li>
        <li>Only approved partners can check your BonID, and every check is recorded.</li>
        <li>If you break these rules, we can close your account.</li>
        <li>Questions? Write to <a href="mailto:support@verifyem.ht" class="text-primary fw-semibold">support@verifyem.ht</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="terms-content">

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">1. Agreeing to these terms</h3>
        <p>
          When you use BonID, you agree to these terms. This includes our website, our apps, our APIs,
          and any other BonID service. If you do not agree, please do not use BonID.
        </p>
        <p>
          These terms apply to everyone: citizens, members of the diaspora, visitors, business partners,
          and law enforcement officers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">2. What BonID is</h3>
        <p>
          BonID is a digital identity platform for Haiti, run by Verifyem. It checks who you are by
          comparing a live photo of your face with your identity document. It also makes sure the photo
          comes from a real person in front of the camera.
        </p>
        <p>
          BonID is <strong>not</strong> a government office. It does not replace your official Haitian
          documents, such as your national identity card (CIN).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">3. Who can use BonID</h3>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>You must be 18 years old or older to open an account.</li>
          <li>You must be a Haitian citizen, a member of the Haitian diaspora, or a visitor to Haiti.</li>
          <li>Businesses must be legally registered.</li>
          <li>Law enforcement accounts need valid PNH credentials and our approval.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">4. Your account and getting verified</h3>
        <p>To get your BonID, you will:</p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Give us true and complete information about yourself.</li>
          <li>Show a valid official identity document, such as your CIN or your passport.</li>
          <li>Show a proof of address.</li>
          <li>Take a live selfie, so we know you are a real person.</li>
          <li>Let us compare your selfie with the photo on your document.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You are in charge of keeping your account safe. Do not share your login codes with anyone.
          If you think someone else got into your account, tell us right away at
          <a href="mailto:support@verifyem.ht" class="text-primary fw-semibold">support@verifyem.ht</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">5. What you must not do</h3>
        <p>You agree that you will not:</p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Use fake, stolen, or changed documents, or documents made with AI.</li>
          <li>Pretend to be someone else, or use another person's face or data.</li>
          <li>Try to trick or get around our live selfie check.</li>
          <li>Use BonID for fraud, money laundering, or anything illegal.</li>
          <li>Try to copy, take apart, or pull data out of BonID systems.</li>
          <li>Use bots or other automatic tools on BonID.</li>
          <li>Share, sell, or give your BonID account or QR code to someone else.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you do any of these things, we may close your account right away, ban you for good,
          and report you to Haitian law enforcement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">6. Your BonID QR code</h3>
        <p>Once you are verified, you get your own BonID number and QR code. Here is how your QR code works:</p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>It is not a simple ID card. Each scan checks your identity live and securely.</li>
          <li>Only approved BonID partners can read it.</li>
          <li>Scanning it does not show your full documents.</li>
          <li>If you think someone is misusing it, you can cancel it and get a new one at any time.</li>
          <li>Every scan is recorded and watched for abuse, and the number of scans is limited.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">7. Rules for partners</h3>
        <p>Businesses, banks, and law enforcement agencies that connect to BonID must:</p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Apply first, and wait for our approval before using BonID.</li>
          <li>Keep their API keys and tokens secret. Never post them in public.</li>
          <li>Follow all Haitian and international laws that protect personal data.</li>
          <li>Look at a person's data only when that person has agreed to the check.</li>
          <li>Tell us right away about any security problem or misuse.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">8. Credits and payment</h3>
        <p>
          Partners pay only for what they use. They buy credits, and each verification uses credits.
          Credits you have used cannot be refunded. Credits you have not used never expire.
          Prices and credit packages may change, and we will tell you before they do.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">9. Our name, brand, and technology</h3>
        <p>
          The BonID name, logo, design, software, and technology belong to Verifyem.
          You may not copy, share, or use them without our written permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">10. Limits on our responsibility</h3>
        <p>
          We work hard to make BonID accurate and secure, but we provide it "as is."
          Verifyem is not responsible for:
        </p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Decisions other people or businesses make based on a BonID check.</li>
          <li>Service outages caused by power, internet problems, or events outside our control.</li>
          <li>Losses that happen because you did not keep your account safe.</li>
          <li>Wrong results caused by blurry or poor quality photos or documents.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">11. Closing an account</h3>
        <p>
          We may pause or close your account if you break these terms, or if you put the safety of
          BonID or its users at risk.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also ask us to delete your account at any time. Just write to
          <a href="mailto:support@verifyem.ht" class="text-primary fw-semibold">support@verifyem.ht</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">12. Which laws apply</h3>
        <p>
          These terms follow the laws of the Republic of Haiti. If there is a legal dispute about BonID,
          it will be handled by the courts of Port-au-Prince, Haiti.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">13. Changes to these terms</h3>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. If we make an important change, we will tell you
          by email or with a message in your account. If you keep using BonID after a change, it means
          you accept the new terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">14. Contact us</h3>
        <p>Have a question about these terms? We are happy to help.</p>
        <ul class="terms-list" style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0;">
